   "text": "I read the drawing as a macrocyclic indole\u2013oxazole\u2013piperazic ester carrying an acylated fluoropyrrolidine side chain.\n\n**Fragments**\n- **Indole:** N-ethyl, with the C2 position bearing a pyridin-3-yl group. That pyridine has a 1-methoxyethyl group at its 2-position. The indole C3 carries a CH2\u2013C(CH3)2\u2013CH2\u2013O ester linkage.\n- **Piperazic ester:** the ester carbonyl is attached to C3 of a hexahydropyridazine ring. The ring N1 is acylated by the amino-acid carbonyl.\n- **Linker to indole:** that amino acid's side chain is CH2 leading to C2 of an oxazole, whose C5 attaches to indole C5, closing the macrocycle.\n- **Valine unit:** the amino acid's NH is acylated by an N-methyl valine.\n- **Side chain:** the N-methyl valine nitrogen is acylated by a 3-fluoropyrrolidine-3-carbonyl group. The pyrrolidine nitrogen carries C(=O)\u2013C\u2261C\u2013C(CH3)2\u2013(azetidin-1-yl).\n\n**Stereocentres**\n\nI assigned each from the wedges and hashes using CIP priorities, then converted to SMILES chirality tags.\n\n| Centre | Configuration |\n|---|---|\n| CH(OMe)CH3 on the pyridine | S |\n| Piperazic C3 | S |\n| Amino-acid \u03b1-carbon | S |\n| Valine \u03b1-carbon | S |\n| Fluoropyrrolidine C3 | R |\n\nThe bold bond at the pyridine C3 is not a stereocentre, so it carries no stereo tag. The fluoropyrrolidine assignment assumes the carbonyl bond is hashed and the C\u2013F bond is a wedge, which is how I read the image.\n\nSMILES: CCn1c(-c2cccnc2[C@H](C)OC)c2CC(C)(C)COC(=O)[C@@H]3CCCN(N3)C(=O)[C@@H](NC(=O)[C@H](C(C)C)N(C)C(=O)[C@@]4(F)CCN(C4)C(=O)C#CC(C)(C)N5CCC5)Cc6ncc(o6)-c7ccc1c2c7"
